            <div class="details">
                <section>
                    <h3 id="stay-title">Where to stay</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Bangkok: party hostels near Khao San Road, or quieter guesthouses in Rambuttri</li>
                        <li>Koh Phangan: beach bungalows in Haad Rin. Book weeks ahead for Full Moon week</li>
                        <li>Siem Reap: hostels near Pub Street, many with pools</li>
                        <li>Hanoi: Old Quarter hostels, walking distance to Beer Street</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <aside>
                    <h3 id="glance-title">At a glance</h3>
                    <div class="glance">
                        <p><strong>Best time:</strong> November to April, the dry season. Check the lunar calendar so you are on Koh Phangan for the full moon.</p>
                        <p><strong>Daily budget:</strong> About $40–60 per person per day. Thailand is the most expensive stop and Cambodia the cheapest.</p>
                        <p><strong>Getting around:</strong> Trains, overnight buses, ferries and cheap regional flights (AirAsia, VietJet).</p>
                        <p><strong>Fly in / fly out:</strong> Arrive in Bangkok (BKK) and leave from Hanoi (HAN).</p>
                    </div>
                </aside>
